WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.954
"What Causes Wrinkles?"

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.840
How are wrinkles formed?

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.260
Their origin and nature is said
to be "notoriously complex,"

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.080
but current thinking
is that wrinkles occur

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.720
where fault lines
develop in aging skin.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.320
The process has been compared
to an old leather glove,

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.820
made out of skin after all,

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.400
that develops creases
at the joints

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.900
due to repetitive stress.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.480
In the face,
the repeated flexion

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.100
may be due
to facial expression.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.440
An 8-year longitudinal study

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.300
found that you can predict
the pattern

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.560
of persistent wrinkles

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.620
by superimposing
upon your resting face

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.860
the expression lines,
temporary wrinkles,

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.880
that form when you smile.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.880
Over time,
the skin folding

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.620
caused by
everyday facial expressions

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.040
etches the temporary grooves
into permanent wrinkles.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:57.000
See how the smile lines
around the eyes at baseline

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.340
show up as permanent wrinkles
8 years later?

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.420
Given that wrinkles develop
from forehead furrows

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.580
and expression lines
from frowns and laughter,

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.520
one dermatology journal review
on aging skin

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.940
offered the tongue in
unwrinkled-cheek suggestion

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.840
of "Living alone to minimize
the use of facial expressions."

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.760
And while you're at it
you could

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.160
"live in space to avoid
the effects of gravity."

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.300
However, there is a way
to freeze parts of your face

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:28.440
into an expressionless mask:
Botox.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.980
In fact, one contraindication
to getting Botox

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.120
is having a job that

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.820
"necessitates a wide range
of facial expressions."

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.640
It's never been
formally put to the test,

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.240
but there was a case report
of a pair of identical twins,

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:45.720
one of whom who spent
tens of thousands of dollars

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.780
getting Botox treatments across
multiple areas on her face

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.400
a few times each year
for 13 years.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.360
Compared to her
non-regularly injected twin,

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.760
she ended up with
fewer imprinted facial lines.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.480
A paper entitled
"Sleep Wrinkles"

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.820
tried to make the case
that wrinkles may result

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.120
from the skin distortion
from mechanical compression

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.140
sleeping on your side.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.340
Of course, the primary author
also is a partner in a company

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.840
selling $160 quote-unquote
"wrinkle-fighting" pillows.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.020
It turns out there does not
appear to be any correlation

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.520
between sleep position
preference

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.640
and the appearance of wrinkles.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.500
Speaking of
questionable products,

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:29.160
what about topical adhesive
"anti-wrinkle" pads

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.020
you paste to your face at night?

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:35.640
Product claims include "look up
to 10-15 years younger,"

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.220
declaring a 70 percent reduction
in wrinkles.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.340
But when actually
put to the test for a month

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.460
for crow's feet, forehead,
or between-the-eye wrinkles,

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:48.600
no objective benefits
were reported at all.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:53.040
There did appear to be a placebo
effect in that subjectively,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.260
the study participants felt
the wrinkles looked better,

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.840
but independent
blinded evaluations

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.480
by facial plastic surgeons
of before-and-after pictures

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.480
showed no significant change.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.900
So what can we do
to prevent wrinkling?

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.300
Some of it is genetics.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.480
For example, having lighter skin
color is a predisposing factor.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.520
Among light skin tones,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.060
Caucasian skin wrinkles more
readily than Asian skin,

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.400
for which aging
is more characterized

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.900
by pigmentation changes

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.140
such as freckles, blotchy
patches, and liver spots.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.000
Among Asian skin types,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.460
Chinese women tend to have
more wrinkles around their eyes

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.420
than Japanese women,

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.400
whereas Thai women
tend to wrinkle more

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.900
in the lower half
of their faces.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.980
There are, however,
factors we have control over.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.880
For example, drier skin has
also been found predictive

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.380
of more persistent wrinkling,

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.280
suggesting regular use
of skin moisturizers may help.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.920
When it comes
to wrinkle formation,

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:52.500
it takes two to tango.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.200
Wrinkles are formed
by repetitive creasing

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.640
of aged skin.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.520
Kids can scrunch their faces
all they want

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.980
because the architecture
of their skin has yet to be

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:03.240
irreparably damaged,

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.860
and the lack of creasing

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.380
is why you don't have
wrinkles on your forearms

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.480
no matter how much sun
they've soaked up.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.260
Rather than immobilizing
your face with Botox,

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:17.280
you can focus on preventing
the underlying structural damage

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.780
that makes your skin
susceptible.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:23.640
This involves tobacco avoidance
and regular sun protection.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.020
What about safeguarding
against other kinds of light?

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.860
From the Journal of Biomedical
Physics and Engineering:

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:35.160
"Can light emitted
from smartphone screens

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:38.880
and taking selfies cause
premature aging and wrinkles?"

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.740
Human skin cells bathed in
the light of iPhones and iPads

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.640
experienced an 80 to 90 percent
increase in free radicals,

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.500
compared to shielded
control cells,

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.740
suggesting electronic device
generated light

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.080
"may be harmful to skin."

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.860
Now, on one hand,
they positioned the screens

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.680
unrealistically close,
one centimeter,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:04.560
resulting in about
10 times the irradiance

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.480
compared to a reading distance
of about a foot.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.840
On the other hand,
the skin cells were only exposed

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:13.140
for an unrealistically
short time, only an hour.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.380
The researchers called
for future studies

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:19.380
to evaluate the impact
of lower, longer doses

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.900
on skin outcomes
such as collagen deposition.

